[#:seon.task{:name "a-config-read-rebuilds-the-packaged-projection"
             :kind :function
             :intent "Make `seon.config/effective` reuse the held program's declaration information instead of asking `seon.config/declared-projection` to rebuild `seon.schema/declaration-projection` from `seon.schema.edn/packaged-forms` after central cache eviction. H9's cold SCI sample performs 3,604 `seon.schema/contract-references` walks (253 ms self) and 217 schema-resource reads through this config path; `seon.sci.eval/derive-base-ctx` itself performs zero walks and copies armed roots. Preserve branch-local dials, newer loaded-program dials and the existing shipped-default semantics; no second cache or per-call packaged population build. Red proof `seon.sci.acquisition-cost-test/a-config-read-reuses-its-carried-projection` measures `seon.config/effective` with the database and carried projection already held after emptying seon.cache in a check JVM, requiring zero reference walks and resource reads. H10's retained-contract arming optimization does not reach this path."
             :must-read #{seon.config/effective seon.config/effective-in seon.config/declared-projection
                          seon.schema/declaration-projection seon.schema.edn/packaged-forms
                          seon.sci.acquisition-cost-test/a-config-read-reuses-its-carried-projection}
             :evidence #{"docs/research/agent-platform/2026-10-11/start-a-flow-benchmark.md"}}
